From: WT9103 bring-up
Subject: [PATCH] net: ethernet: mtk_wed: disable RX capability on NRadio WT9103

NRadio WT9103 (MT7981, WED v2) can keep WED attached for TX acceleration
but is unstable with the WED v2 RX datapath enabled. The failure shows up
as mt7915 TX free notification parsing warnings followed by random memory
corruption crashes under sustained eth1 <-> Wi-Fi traffic.

Make the workaround strictly device-specific by matching the board
compatible string. Other MT7981/MT7986 WED v2 devices keep the existing
RX capability behavior.

--- a/include/linux/soc/mediatek/mtk_wed.h
+++ b/include/linux/soc/mediatek/mtk_wed.h
@@ -5,6 +5,7 @@
 #include <linux/rcupdate.h>
 #include <linux/regmap.h>
 #include <linux/pci.h>
+#include <linux/of.h>
 #include <linux/skbuff.h>
 #include <linux/netdevice.h>
 
@@ -251,8 +252,11 @@ mtk_wed_device_attach(struct mtk_wed_dev
 
 static inline bool mtk_wed_get_rx_capa(struct mtk_wed_device *dev)
 {
 #ifdef CONFIG_NET_MEDIATEK_SOC_WED
+	if (of_machine_is_compatible("nradio,wt9103"))
+		return false;
+
 	if (dev->version == 3)
 		return dev->wlan.hw_rro;
 
